tring-name>, <string-name><surname>Serrurier</surname> <given-names>B</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Dard&#x000e9;</surname> <given-names>ML</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Carme</surname> <given-names>B</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Atypical <italic>Toxoplasma gondii</italic> strain from a free-living jaguar (<italic>Panthera onca</italic>) in French Guiana.</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source> <year>2008</year>;<volume>78</volume>:<fpage>195</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18256411</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Howe</surname> <given-names>DK</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Sibley</surname> <given-names>LD</given-names></string-name> <article-title><italic>Toxoplasma gondii</italic> comprises three clonal lineages: correlation of parasite genotype with human disease.</article-title><source>J Infect Dis</source> <year>1995</year>;<volume>172</volume>:<fpage>1561</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7594717</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11. </label><citation citation-type="book"><string-name><surname>Emmons</surname> <given-names>LH</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Feer</surname> <given-names>F</given-names></string-name> Neotropical rainforest mammals: a field guide. 2nd ed. Chicago: The University of Chicago Press; <year>1999</year></citation></ref><ref id="R12"><label>12. </label><citation citation-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Lehmann</surname> <given-names>T</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Marcet</surname> <given-names>PL</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Graham</surname> <given-names>DH</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Dahl</surname> <given-names>ER</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Dubey</surname> <given-names>JP</given-names></string-na